--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -18,11 +18,16 @@ Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "c
 | `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
 | `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
 | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
 
-Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
+Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`:
+
+- 400 `title is required`: `title` is missing, not a string, or blank (on `POST`, and on `PATCH` when the body has a `title`).
+- 400 `title must be at most 200 characters`: checked after trimming; titles are saved trimmed.
+- 400 `invalid JSON body`: the body does not parse.
+- 500 `internal error`: anything unexpected; the details are logged on the server only.
 
 ## Layout
 
 - `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied).
 - `src/tasks.ts`: the queries.
